3 NOTE Thanks so much for sharing this. I like to have as many certificates as I can on all of my family members, he being my 17x cousin, 8x removed! God bless you for the sharing of this document! 
3 NOTE As far as I can see no cause of death is discernible in the document but I remember many years ago a study  was done on his remains and poison was found in the roots of his hair or in the hair itself which indicated that his death
4 CONC  was due to poisoning. I think it was arsenic as apposed to cyanide but I can't be sure.
