1 NAME Giuseppe Niccolò /Spada-Veralli/ I principe di Castel Viscardo
2 GIVN Giuseppe Niccolò
2 SURN Spada-Veralli
2 NSFX I principe di Castel Viscardo
2 _MARNM Spada-Veralli
1 NAME Giuseppe Niccolò Spada Veralli, principe di Castelviscardo
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1752
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1840
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1763, Pope Clement XIII authorized him to use the Spada Veralli surname and coat of arms. His title of Marchese was changed at his own request to that of Prince of Castel Viscardo by Pius VI in 1777 on the occas
2 CONC ion of his marriage to Giacinta Ruspoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1798, when the French were reorganizing much of Italy, Prince Giuseppe Spada was one of a group of aristocrats who espoused republicanism and welcomed the new order. The French occupied Rome on 11 February 1798 and on the same 
2 CONC day, with the agreement of General Berthier, Prince Giuseppe Spada was appointed a member of the Congregation of State together with three Cardinals and two other laymen, all considered favourable to the French. As Citizen Spada, 
2 CONC he commanded the national guard in the period February June 1798. He became a Senator of Rome and was appointed to the French Senate in the Palais Luxembourg. Although Giuseppe lived in Rome, his attention was fixed on Bologna, wh
2 CONC ere his heir, Clemente, was born the year after his marriage. He bought the Palazzo Zagnoni in Bologna in 1802 and transferred there with his family in that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spada_Veralli err.
2 CONT
