1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Birth and parents ==
2 CONT * Birth / Baptism ('''primary'''): 28 June 1850, Eggby parish, Skaraborgs län, Västergötland, Sweden
2 CONT ** Details: Correct birth date stated as 28 June 1850 in the birth and baptism record.
2 CONT ** References: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/C0053257_00012 Eggby i Varnhems kyrkoarkiv, Födelse- och dopböcker, SE/GLA/13612/C/4 (1850-1871), bildid C0053257_00012, sida 11]
2 CONT * Birth ('''compiled'''): 27 June 1850, Eggby parish, Skaraborgs län, Västergötland, Sweden
2 CONT ** Details: Alternate birth date stated in Sveriges Dödbok.
2 CONT ** References: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/173619303/person/132255532317 Ancestry Genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Ebba Albertina Björling, born Stålhane, was born in Eggby parish, Skaraborgs län, in June 1850. Her birth date is clearly stated as 28 June 1850 in the contemporary birth and baptism record ('''primary'''), while Sveriges Dödbok g
2 CONC ives 27 June 1850 ('''compiled'''), representing a minor discrepancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT She spent her childhood and youth in several Skaraborg parishes, including Eggby, Öglunda, Lerdala, Böja, and Björsäter, as shown by household examination books ('''compiled''' via ArkivDigital references). These records indicate 
2 CONC continuous residence in parental or family households through the 1860s and 1870s.
2 CONT
2 CONT By the late 1870s she appears in Stockholm, first in Hedvig Eleonora parish ('''compiled''') and shortly thereafter in the Rotemansarkivet system ('''administrative'''). From 1879 onward, Rotemansarkivet documents a complex sequen
2 CONC ce of residences and administrative transfers across multiple Stockholm rotes, including Tegnérroten (Rote 5), Observatorieroten (Rote 6), Danviksroten (Rote 12), Stadsgårdsroten (Rote 13), Kronobergsroten (Rote 17), Teknologroten
2 CONC  (Rote 18), and Vanadisroten (Rote 21). Several entries explicitly state “kvarstår”, indicating administrative copying of records without physical relocation.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Carl Fredrik Björling on 12 October 1873 ('''compiled'''). During the early 1890s she lived with her husband and children in Nacka parish at Fannys Udde ('''compiled''' household examination), followed by renewed resid
2 CONC ence in Stockholm. Her final recorded residence was in Johannes parish, Stockholm, where she died on 8 May 1903; Rotemansarkivet records death as the reason for removal ('''administrative'''; '''compiled''' via Sveriges Dödbok).
2 CONT
2 CONT Claims of a relationship with Oscar II, King of Sweden and Norway, appear only in user trees/SmartCopy material in earlier pasted data and remain an '''unverified lead''' due to lack of supporting primary or administrative evidenc
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
