0 @N6000000002322348682@ NOTE He was the 3rd son of Napoleon I's brother Louis, king of Holland (1806-10).
1 CONT He gave his country 2 decades of prosperity under a stable, authoritarian
1 CONT government, but finally led it to defeat in the Franco-German War (1870-71).
1 CONT Living much of his life in exile, he finally re-entered France to be elected
1 CONT as its first President of the Second Republic. He desolved the legislature
1 CONT because of a one-term presidency and became Emperor of France. He was later
1 CONT deposed on Sept-04-1870 and the Third Republic was declared.
